@bank all
// SW3 (2026-10-26, Pillar 5 Step 5, S5-3 words; spec section 10): M19 Power and relays (24v). The training is meeting
// train.m19.calder in the relay room (Deck 1, u); Calder's step words are her own `work` lines, flags train.m19.*; the
// crew's answers in the drill are content/banks/m19.lines. Said by nobody unless noted. No "!". Mails "Subject | body".

== works.mech.m19
- Power and relays
// the ask ({time}, {place} filled by the game)
== works.ask.m19
- Power and relays | Your first Senior training. The relay room, Deck 1. Bring your hands; I'll bring the relays. {time}, {place}.
== next.m19
- Power and relays comes next: the relay room on Deck 1, with the Chief.
== next.wait.m19
- Power and relays: meet the Chief in the relay room, Deck 1.
// the ring on the relay room's door, and the notice 30 minutes before
== m19.ptr
- Power and relays with Calder, {time}
== m19.notice
- Power and relays with the Chief at {time}: the relay room, Deck 1. Go at quarter to.

// the relay panel (a bridge relay rack: 1-relay-1, 1-relay-2), tapped
== m19.relay.title
- Relay rack · {machine}
== m19.relay.look
- Twelve relays in a row. One light is slow to come on.
== m19.relay.pull
- Pull the slow one
== m19.relay.seat
- Seat the new relay
== m19.relay.test
- Test the rack
== m19.relay.done
- All twelve lights come on together. The bridge won't flicker.
== m19.relay.wrong
- That one's fine. Watch the lights again: which is slow?
// the battery rows (Deck 5, y: 5-battery-1 to -4), tapped
== m19.battery.title
- Battery bank · {machine}
== m19.battery.read
- Charge: {n} in a hundred.
== m19.battery.low
- This bank is lower than the others.
== m19.battery.even
- All four banks within two of each other. Balanced.
== m19.battery.balance
- Balance the banks
== m19.battery.done
- The banks share the load evenly now.
// stage 2: a conduit run with the conduit tester (6-conduit-1, -2)
== m19.conduit.title
- Conduit run · {machine}
== m19.conduit.test
- Test this length
== m19.conduit.good
- Clean all the way. Next length.
== m19.conduit.fault
- The tester drops here. The fault is in this length.
// the tester given (toast; only if M15 hasn't given it)
== m19.tester.give
- The Chief gave you a conduit tester. It's in your locker.
== m19.trained.stage2
- Power and relays: you can test conduit runs now.
== m19.trained.stage3
- Power and relays: you can balance the battery banks now.

// the drill (Wednesdays 15:00, once you're Senior): you run the Works part. The ring, the card, your calls
== drill.works.ptr
- Run the Works part of the drill
== drill.works.title
- The drill: Works
== drill.works.text
- You call Works' part. Three calls, in order. The crew answer on their devices.
== drill.works.call.1
- Works: all hands to your stations.
== drill.works.call.2
- Isolate the non-essential power. Report when done.
== drill.works.call.3
- Head count. Works, report in.
== drill.works.done
- Works reports all present and safe. Drill time: {time}.
== drill.works.order
- Not yet. Stations first, then power, then the count.
